courses.learning_outcomes:
By living and studying at an overseas institution, the students will be able to:
• gain exposure to a different legal system and broaden their visions in legal study;
• develop skills in cross-cultural communication;
• gain knowledge and insights into another jurisdiction’s legal system and its distinctiveness from the law of Hong Kong; and
• develop an understanding of the history, policy and culture of another country.

By the end of this course, students will be able to:

• Explain the historical and political factors that led to the creation of the WTO;
• Describe the structure, main functions, and key agreements of the WTO;
• Outline the fundamental principles that guide international trade law in the WTO context;
• Analyze the impact of WTO rules and dispute settlement on global trade and diplomacy;
• Evaluate the role of the WTO in regional contexts, particularly in Hong Kong and Mainland China;
• Identify the contemporary challenges facing the WTO and the possible paths for reform;
• Apply knowledge of trade governance to real-world situations from the perspectives of governments, international organizations, and the private sector;
• Develop basic research and critical thinking skills relevant to international trade law and policy.

By the end of this course, students will be able to:

• Demonstrate a sound understanding of international legal doctrines discussed in the class and formulate legal arguments on their basis;
• Understand the nature of international law and be able to theorise as to its viability as a law form;
• Distinguish between international law and municipal law and understand the several philosophies relating to this relationship;
• Comprehend the role of international law in international politics and governance.

By living and studying at the top law school in America, the students will

* gain exposure to different legal system and broaden their visions in legal study;
* develop skills in cross-cultural communication;
* gain knowledge and insights into America’s legal system and its approach to American law; and

develop an understanding of the history, politics and culture of America.

